        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>72yo F referred for polypharmacy review. Currently on 9 prescription medications with multiple documented drug-drug interactions and adverse events over past 6 months: 1) NSAID+warfarin → GI bleed, 2) Omeprazole+clopidogrel → reduced clopidogrel efficacy → MI, 3) Atorvastatin+diltiazem → rhabdomyolysis+AKI, 4) SSRI+anticoagulants → increased bleeding risk, 5) Mirtazapine → weight gain+worsened HTN. Patient confused about medication changes, reports taking 'old pills' she found. BEERS Criteria concerns: Multiple CNS-active drugs (mirtazapine+metoprolol), anticoagulation in elderly with CKD and prior bleed, anticholinergic burden. Fall risk elevated. Cognitive screening shows MoCA 22/30 (mild impairment). Recommend: 1) Medication simplification, 2) Pill organizer and home health, 3) Consider DOAC vs warfarin (but CKD limits options), 4) Deprescribing non-essential meds.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
